You should run a ping for longer than 7 seconds to get useful info,
really.

I've just run 5 minutes of ping to nethack.alt.org, and got no dropped
packets at all. No obvious trouble while telnetting either, so it's
presumably a problem on the route either from you to nao or the route
back.

>With the exception of my own router, traceroute doesn't show the nodes,
>just stars for all hops.

Your router is probably blocking ICMP (which you might be able to
change), or your ISP's first router is (which you won't).

> So I asked a friend who provided these data...

Even if your friend very very local (like next door) and using the
same ISP, odds are that they get a significantly different route and
may bypass the problematic link. 

